    "l02 and l03 start at the calling function rather than at a variable: the values 3 and 5 are literals at the call site, so the caller is the origin of the value.",
    "`bumped` is rebound inside the `if`, so the second binding is its own node, `bumped#2`. One node with a self-edge would put `factor` and `value` in the backward slice of the offset-adjusted result even on the path where the `if` did not run.",
    "Both bindings reach `return bumped`: #2 when the offset was applied, #1 when it was not. Two RETURNS edges, not one -- picking either alone would drop a real path."
